00:00:35.357 --> 00:00:37.921
Everything else I'm just
rubbing sticks together, man.

00:00:37.921 --> 00:00:39.006
- Just goldfish brain.

00:00:39.006 --> 00:00:42.162
- Yeah man, I just can't fathom
anything else in my life.

00:00:42.162 --> 00:00:42.995
So what can I do?

00:00:42.995 --> 00:00:44.365
I'm useless, man.

00:00:44.365 --> 00:00:47.286
Shout out to everyone who
defended me for my monkey brain.

00:00:47.286 --> 00:00:49.458
Today I want to talk about, fellas,

00:00:49.458 --> 00:00:51.221
I had a thought last night.

00:00:51.221 --> 00:00:52.888
I was like, wow,

00:00:52.888 --> 00:00:54.353
I've got my life together.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:57.302
(laughing)

00:00:57.302 --> 00:00:59.008
- We all know that's a lie.

00:00:59.008 --> 00:01:00.181
No one just thinks that.

00:01:00.181 --> 00:01:01.307
- Okay, okay.

00:01:01.307 --> 00:01:03.068
I've got my life more
together than before.

00:01:03.068 --> 00:01:03.990
- [Joey] Yeah, yeah.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.038
That's better.

00:01:05.038 --> 00:01:05.871
- And I was wondering.

00:01:05.871 --> 00:01:06.704
I'm like, well,

00:01:06.704 --> 00:01:09.452
I've had a drastic life
change from moving to Japan.

00:01:09.452 --> 00:01:11.278
And that's not because of
anything to do with Japan,

00:01:11.278 --> 00:01:13.636
that's purely because of I think the fact

00:01:13.636 --> 00:01:16.285
that someone's holding me accountable.

00:01:16.285 --> 00:01:18.648
Before, if I fucked up a sponsor,

00:01:18.648 --> 00:01:19.481
it was on me.

00:01:19.481 --> 00:01:21.788
But now there's someone else involved.

00:01:21.788 --> 00:01:23.484
I was wondering, 'cause I'll explain mine,

00:01:23.484 --> 00:01:26.362
but did you, you know when
you guys moved to Japan,

00:01:26.362 --> 00:01:28.270
and you know, maybe when
you joined the agency?

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:29.225
Did your life change that much,

00:01:29.225 --> 00:01:31.300
did you have a lifestyle change

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.910
or was it just the same shit?

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.592
- I think the biggest
change for me has been,

00:01:34.592 --> 00:01:36.165
actually, this podcast.

00:01:36.165 --> 00:01:39.167
Where we have a specific
day we come in and film,

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:41.363
and having something on my schedule

00:01:41.363 --> 00:01:43.945
has just completely changed
my entire weekly schedule,

00:01:43.945 --> 00:01:46.400
just because I have one day
that's always booked off,

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.105
and I have to plan around
that instead of being like,

00:01:49.105 --> 00:01:50.781
I'm gonna wake up and I'm gonna feel,

00:01:50.781 --> 00:01:53.047
like, maybe I'll feel like
working on something today,

00:01:53.047 --> 00:01:56.998
maybe I'll just feel like
playing Ghost of Tsushima.

00:01:56.998 --> 00:01:57.831
I don't fucking know.

00:01:57.831 --> 00:01:58.705
- There's nothing worse I feel

00:01:58.705 --> 00:02:00.952
than it being a Monday morning,

00:02:00.952 --> 00:02:01.785
right?

00:02:01.785 --> 00:02:02.973
It's a fresh start to a new week,

00:02:02.973 --> 00:02:04.024
and you're like, alright,

00:02:04.024 --> 00:02:05.069
let's see what I have to do this week.

00:02:05.069 --> 00:02:07.239
And you look on your calender,
it's just nothing this week.

00:02:07.239 --> 00:02:08.072
(laughing)

00:02:08.072 --> 00:02:10.570
I'm just like, what do I do?

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.447
How do I do things now?

00:02:12.447 --> 00:02:13.992
- Especially after quarantine!

00:02:13.992 --> 00:02:15.606
You just wake up and you don't even

00:02:15.606 --> 00:02:17.083
know what day of the week it is,

00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:19.106
and weekends don't feel like weekends,

00:02:19.106 --> 00:02:21.588
weekdays are just other
days, I don't know.

00:02:21.588 --> 00:02:22.752
- Yeah, most people wake up being like,

00:02:22.752 --> 00:02:23.585
oh, yes,

00:02:23.585 --> 00:02:24.744
it's a Friday, it's the end of the week.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:25.728
I just wake up, it's like,

00:02:25.728 --> 00:02:27.461
it is morning.
(rooster crowing)

00:02:27.461 --> 00:02:29.634
- A YouTuber's everyday is the same day.

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:30.961
- Yeah, it is.

00:02:30.961 --> 00:02:33.424
- When everyone started working from home,

00:02:33.424 --> 00:02:34.257
and everyone was like,

00:02:34.257 --> 00:02:35.090
oh, yes,

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:37.509
this is such a refreshing
change to my lifestyle!

00:02:37.509 --> 00:02:38.670
- And we're just like yeah.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.791
- Yeah, welcome to the YouTuber lifestyle.

00:02:40.791 --> 00:02:42.008
- I mean, it's fun when
everyone's doing it,

00:02:42.008 --> 00:02:43.260
and everyone's in the same boat.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.115
But then when everyone's doing

00:02:45.115 --> 00:02:46.630
their normal life and working,

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:47.514
it's like it's hell.

00:02:47.514 --> 00:02:49.197
- That's how I felt though,

00:02:49.197 --> 00:02:50.619
like when we, as you said,

00:02:50.619 --> 00:02:52.421
we started to be like, alright,

00:02:52.421 --> 00:02:53.840
every week, this day,

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.183
this time, we're gonna
come to the studio--

00:02:55.183 --> 00:02:56.357
- Yeah, it's really nice.

00:02:56.357 --> 00:02:57.190
I do like that.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.526
- And it's like (sighs quickly),

00:02:58.526 --> 00:03:00.292
this is how normal people feel.

00:03:00.292 --> 00:03:02.657
This is quite liberating,
I kind of like it--

00:03:02.657 --> 00:03:03.667
- I drink coffee with other people.

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:04.500
- I know!

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:05.371
- No, it's great,

00:03:05.371 --> 00:03:06.526
because, you know,

00:03:06.526 --> 00:03:07.737
when I worked at the BBC,

00:03:07.737 --> 00:03:09.730
I worked there for like two years,

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.521
like close to three years,

00:03:11.521 --> 00:03:14.140
and I did not enjoy it after a while.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.693
But after moving to YouTube
and being freelance,

00:03:16.693 --> 00:03:18.286
and just going by my own schedule,

00:03:18.286 --> 00:03:19.890
I kind of missed the office environment,

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.991
because about a year after doing YouTube,

00:03:22.991 --> 00:03:24.739
I kind of realized, man,

00:03:24.739 --> 00:03:27.995
if I don't actively go out
and seek social interaction,

00:03:27.995 --> 00:03:29.153
it just doesn't happen now.

00:03:29.153 --> 00:03:30.967
- It doesn't happen, yeah.

00:03:30.967 --> 00:03:33.107
That took me like three or
four years to realize that.

00:03:33.107 --> 00:03:33.991
(laughing)

00:03:33.991 --> 00:03:36.139
I was like, do I have no friends?

00:03:36.139 --> 00:03:37.853
(laughing)

00:03:37.853 --> 00:03:38.686
Unless they, like,

00:03:38.686 --> 00:03:39.519
drag me out?

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.439
Like, it's just weird.

00:03:40.439 --> 00:03:41.299
- I kind of, yeah,

00:03:41.299 --> 00:03:42.244
I kind of got that same thing,

00:03:42.244 --> 00:03:44.196
'cause I never had a business,

00:03:44.196 --> 00:03:46.611
like a corporate experience, right?

00:03:46.611 --> 00:03:48.439
Like working in an office or whatever.

00:03:48.439 --> 00:03:51.117
So it's extra exciting for me,

00:03:51.117 --> 00:03:52.064
because I'm just,

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:53.267
'cause it is liberating,

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:54.821
'cause I've always been,
even during school,

00:03:54.821 --> 00:03:56.626
I've always been one of
those kids where it's like,

00:03:56.626 --> 00:03:58.613
I couldn't study on my own.

00:03:58.613 --> 00:03:59.822
Like I had to.

00:03:59.822 --> 00:04:00.655
- Oh, you were one of those.

00:04:00.655 --> 00:04:01.488
- Yeah.

00:04:01.488 --> 00:04:03.874
