00:50:04.004 --> 00:50:04.837
She gave you a note?

00:50:04.837 --> 00:50:05.670
- She gave me like a,

00:50:05.670 --> 00:50:07.461
it's not the one time either,

00:50:07.461 --> 00:50:09.492
that's like the third or
fourth letter she sent me.

00:50:09.492 --> 00:50:10.544
- Can you explain the whole story?

00:50:10.544 --> 00:50:12.767
I'm interested, 'cause I
don't know the timeline.

00:50:12.767 --> 00:50:13.600
- So basically,

00:50:13.600 --> 00:50:14.988
I don't even remember
when the first one was.

00:50:14.988 --> 00:50:16.975
But basically I came home once,

00:50:16.975 --> 00:50:18.058
and in Japan,

00:50:18.982 --> 00:50:20.949
I don't know if it's in
other countries as well,

00:50:20.949 --> 00:50:22.677
but at least in Japan, in apartments,

00:50:22.677 --> 00:50:25.193
they have a mailbox
downstairs on the first floor,

00:50:25.193 --> 00:50:27.515
and they also have a little
mail entry thing on the door?

00:50:27.515 --> 00:50:28.608
- I think that's a normal thing.

00:50:28.608 --> 00:50:29.799
- I think, I don't know.

00:50:29.799 --> 00:50:32.254
But basically I came home and
I was about to open the door,

00:50:32.254 --> 00:50:33.914
and I saw a piece of paper sticking out,

00:50:33.914 --> 00:50:34.747
so I'm like, okay,

00:50:34.747 --> 00:50:35.996
must be a flyer or something.

00:50:35.996 --> 00:50:36.829
- Missed a package.

00:50:36.829 --> 00:50:37.871
- Yeah, missed a package or something.

00:50:37.871 --> 00:50:40.571
And I open it, and it's this really,

00:50:40.571 --> 00:50:41.635
it was really creepy,

00:50:41.635 --> 00:50:44.107
because it's like to nobody,

00:50:44.107 --> 00:50:47.505
it was clearly typed out,
and it was just in English.

00:50:47.505 --> 00:50:48.448
And I read it and I'm like,

00:50:48.448 --> 00:50:50.266
this sounds Google translated.

00:50:50.266 --> 00:50:51.644
And I read it, and it's the woman,

00:50:51.644 --> 00:50:53.362
it's a guy or a woman downstairs.

00:50:53.362 --> 00:50:54.250
I don't even know who it is,

00:50:54.250 --> 00:50:57.621
because when you first move
to an apartment in Japan,

00:50:57.621 --> 00:51:01.441
it's customary to go to
every room that's adjacent.

00:51:01.441 --> 00:51:02.274
- Yep.

00:51:02.274 --> 00:51:03.781
- I'll tell my story about that after--

00:51:03.781 --> 00:51:05.723
- So the two rooms to the
left and right of you,

00:51:05.723 --> 00:51:07.822
and the person below and
above you, if there are any,

00:51:07.822 --> 00:51:09.502
and go and basically say, like,

00:51:09.502 --> 00:51:10.923
hey, I just moved in here.

00:51:10.923 --> 00:51:12.489
You know, if you ever need anything,

00:51:12.489 --> 00:51:14.010
I'm in this room kind of thing.

00:51:14.010 --> 00:51:15.810
The two people to the sides of me?

00:51:15.810 --> 00:51:17.998
Fucking great, I love both my neighbors.

00:51:17.998 --> 00:51:19.129
The woman at the top?

00:51:19.129 --> 00:51:19.962
Super nice.

00:51:19.962 --> 00:51:20.795
Barely talk to her.

00:51:20.795 --> 00:51:22.177
But the woman at the bottom?

00:51:22.177 --> 00:51:24.068
She didn't even come to the door.

00:51:24.068 --> 00:51:25.010
I rung the doorbell.

00:51:25.010 --> 00:51:28.288
I clearly heard her
running up to the door!

00:51:28.288 --> 00:51:29.121
- To look?

00:51:29.121 --> 00:51:30.182
- To look in the peephole.

00:51:30.182 --> 00:51:31.429
- You should have put your
thumb on the peephole.

00:51:31.429 --> 00:51:33.427
- Yeah, and I guarantee,

00:51:33.427 --> 00:51:36.201
the moment that she looked
at the peephole and gaijin

00:51:36.201 --> 00:51:37.727
she was like, oh hell no.

00:51:37.727 --> 00:51:40.438
I'm not going out there,
are you kidding me?

00:51:40.438 --> 00:51:42.904
So immediately I was like, okay.

00:51:42.904 --> 00:51:44.207
I have that kind of neighbor.

00:51:44.207 --> 00:51:45.734
Well, whatever.

00:51:45.734 --> 00:51:46.775
And then, yeah,

00:51:46.775 --> 00:51:48.607
I immediately knew.

00:51:48.607 --> 00:51:49.794
It didn't say in this letter,

00:51:49.794 --> 00:51:50.653
it didn't say--

00:51:50.653 --> 00:51:51.486
- [Connor] Who it was.

00:51:51.486 --> 00:51:52.319
- Who it was,

00:51:52.319 --> 00:51:53.698
but, man.

00:51:53.698 --> 00:51:55.558
She must have not thought this through,

00:51:55.558 --> 00:51:56.682
because in the letter she said,

00:51:56.682 --> 00:51:59.189
I always hear you guys stomping around.

00:51:59.189 --> 00:52:00.022
So I'm like, well,

00:52:00.022 --> 00:52:01.732
clearly you live below me.

00:52:01.732 --> 00:52:03.750
You're not even hiding it now!

00:52:03.750 --> 00:52:05.085
And she's like, yeah,

00:52:05.085 --> 00:52:07.414
your stomping is so loud in the night

00:52:07.414 --> 00:52:09.581
that I'm getting insomnia.

00:52:11.083 --> 00:52:13.211
And I'm just like, okay?

00:52:13.211 --> 00:52:14.566
I mean, sorry?

00:52:14.566 --> 00:52:16.556
Like, you must hate me then,

00:52:16.556 --> 00:52:17.592
in my previous place,

00:52:17.592 --> 00:52:19.574
because I was up till fucking 4AM.

00:52:19.574 --> 00:52:23.084
I'm living a normal
fucking life in this place.

00:52:23.084 --> 00:52:25.382
Yeah, and she kept sending me it,

00:52:25.382 --> 00:52:26.468
and I'm just like, oh my God.

00:52:26.468 --> 00:52:27.535
What am I gonna do with this woman?

00:52:27.535 --> 00:52:30.108
So the moment she sent this recent letter,

00:52:30.108 --> 00:52:31.010
like a couple of weeks ago?

00:52:31.010 --> 00:52:31.878
I was like, you know what?

00:52:31.878 --> 00:52:33.375
I'm gonna fucking show this woman,

00:52:33.375 --> 00:52:34.927
'cause I'm getting fucking annoyed.

00:52:34.927 --> 00:52:35.760
Because she threatened to, like--

00:52:35.760 --> 00:52:37.016
- Burn down her apartment.

00:52:37.016 --> 00:52:38.088
(laughing)

00:52:38.088 --> 00:52:40.016
- So I unscrewed the hinges in her door.

00:52:40.016 --> 00:52:41.046
(laughing)

00:52:41.046 --> 00:52:42.458
- I broke down her door.

00:52:42.458 --> 00:52:43.617
- And threw poop at it.

00:52:43.617 --> 00:52:44.757
(laughing)

00:52:44.757 --> 00:52:45.968
I shat in her mailbox.

00:52:45.968 --> 00:52:47.919
(laughing)

00:52:47.919 --> 00:52:49.418
- Honestly, honestly would have got her.

00:52:49.418 --> 00:52:51.078
I'm joking.

00:52:51.078 --> 00:52:52.518
- No, so I was like,

00:52:52.518 --> 00:52:53.412
I'm gonna show this woman.

00:52:53.412 --> 00:52:54.245
'Cause, like,

00:52:54.245 --> 00:52:56.559
clearly by writing, by typing,

00:52:56.559 --> 00:52:57.611
not even handwriting.

00:52:57.611 --> 00:53:01.023
By typing out a clearly Google
translated letter to me,

00:53:01.023 --> 00:53:02.240
she obviously thinks, like,

00:53:02.240 --> 00:53:04.628
oh, these fucking dumb arse
foreigners don't know anything.

00:53:04.628 --> 00:53:08.916
And there's this mentality of
xenophobic Japanese people,

00:53:08.916 --> 00:53:10.232
usually very senile,

00:53:10.232 --> 00:53:11.981
who think that they can get their way

00:53:11.981 --> 00:53:14.620
because they're a senile Japanese person,

00:53:14.620 --> 00:53:17.630
and we're just a dumb foreigner
who doesn't know the rules.

00:53:17.630 --> 00:53:18.463
So I'm just like, alright.

00:53:18.463 --> 00:53:19.296
I'll show them.

00:53:19.296 --> 00:53:21.991
So I wrote a handwritten
letter, in Japanese,

00:53:21.991 --> 00:53:24.923
in the most Keigo as fuck, like.

00:53:24.923 --> 00:53:26.234
- Businessman Japanese.

00:53:26.234 --> 00:53:28.826
- Yeah, the most polite Japanese
that you could ever see.

00:53:28.826 --> 00:53:31.839
I might as well have written
a fucking invitation letter,

00:53:31.839 --> 00:53:32.672
like a resume--

00:53:32.672 --> 00:53:33.505
- To the King.

00:53:33.505 --> 00:53:35.173
- To the King, right?

00:53:35.173 --> 00:53:36.341
And so I wrote it down,

00:53:36.341 --> 00:53:39.012
and I basically said I'm
sorry but we gotta do it,

00:53:39.012 --> 00:53:41.705
because I work sometimes late at night,

00:53:41.705 --> 00:53:43.840
and we're not trying to
be noisy or whatever,

00:53:43.840 --> 00:53:44.718
and it's like,

00:53:44.718 --> 00:53:46.317
and I basically said at
the bottom, I was like,

00:53:46.317 --> 00:53:48.500
rather than you taking it to the housing

00:53:48.500 --> 00:53:50.177
company and try and threaten me,

00:53:50.177 --> 00:53:53.103
maybe we should talk face to face?

00:53:53.103 --> 00:53:54.752
Which is basically the most passive

00:53:54.752 --> 00:53:56.235
aggressive way of saying come at me,

00:53:56.235 --> 00:53:57.068
bitch.

00:53:57.943 --> 00:53:59.681
Fucking meet me outside.

00:53:59.681 --> 00:54:00.710
Like, come at me.

00:54:00.710 --> 00:54:02.149
- I've been to your
house, you don't stomp.

00:54:02.149 --> 00:54:02.982
- [Joey] No, we don't!

00:54:02.982 --> 00:54:04.050
- You walk like pretty normal--

00:54:04.050 --> 00:54:05.786
- And it was really rude as well.

00:54:05.786 --> 00:54:06.866
She wrote down being like,

00:54:06.866 --> 00:54:08.539
