00:58:15.406 --> 00:58:16.239
(laughing)

00:58:16.239 --> 00:58:17.072
- In capacity.

00:58:17.072 --> 00:58:17.985
(laughing)

00:58:17.985 --> 00:58:18.818
- I remember, actually,

00:58:18.818 --> 00:58:20.212
the first time I went to America,

00:58:20.212 --> 00:58:21.415
I was in New York,

00:58:21.415 --> 00:58:24.418
and this was my very first
experience in America,

00:58:24.418 --> 00:58:26.460
'cause I'd pretty much
only been in England,

00:58:26.460 --> 00:58:28.503
and basically Europe, and Thailand.

00:58:28.503 --> 00:58:31.520
So I remember I was standing
in the lift of my hotel,

00:58:31.520 --> 00:58:32.353
and this American,

00:58:32.353 --> 00:58:34.367
there was one other person in the lift,

00:58:34.367 --> 00:58:35.942
and she asked me, so,

00:58:35.942 --> 00:58:37.375
how are you doing today?

00:58:37.375 --> 00:58:38.440
You having a good day?

00:58:38.440 --> 00:58:40.370
And me, as a British person,

00:58:40.370 --> 00:58:41.768
I fucking freeze up.

00:58:41.768 --> 00:58:43.445
Like, I don't know how to act!

00:58:43.445 --> 00:58:45.980
I'm like, are you picking a fight with me?

00:58:45.980 --> 00:58:46.865
(laughing)

00:58:46.865 --> 00:58:47.947
What the fuck's going here?

00:58:47.947 --> 00:58:49.379
What do you want from me?

00:58:49.379 --> 00:58:50.929
Are you trying to sell something?

00:58:50.929 --> 00:58:52.855
Because in England you
don't talk to each other.

00:58:52.855 --> 00:58:55.346
Everyone stands there in awkward silence

00:58:55.346 --> 00:58:56.783
and doesn't acknowledge each other,

00:58:56.783 --> 00:58:58.825
and we go about our day.

00:58:58.825 --> 00:59:01.299
- I had the same thing
in Canada, on a bus,

00:59:01.299 --> 00:59:03.285
I was 17 maybe?

00:59:03.285 --> 00:59:04.581
I was on a bus, and the guy said,

00:59:04.581 --> 00:59:06.321
like, great weather,

00:59:06.321 --> 00:59:07.527
I'm not doing the accent.

00:59:07.527 --> 00:59:08.360
- [Garnt And Joey] Yeah.

00:59:08.360 --> 00:59:09.193
- Great weather today.

00:59:09.193 --> 00:59:10.026
And I just ignored him.

00:59:10.026 --> 00:59:10.958
(laughing)

00:59:10.958 --> 00:59:13.132
'Cause I didn't think
he was talking to me.

00:59:13.132 --> 00:59:14.168
And then he was like,

00:59:14.168 --> 00:59:15.418
not much of a talker, hey?

00:59:15.418 --> 00:59:16.684
And then I did, like,

00:59:16.684 --> 00:59:21.209
you know how Elle stares
at Light in The Thing?

00:59:21.209 --> 00:59:22.042
I was like.

00:59:22.042 --> 00:59:23.388
(laughing)

00:59:23.388 --> 00:59:25.392
Like, you talking to me?

00:59:25.392 --> 00:59:27.830
(laughing)

00:59:27.830 --> 00:59:30.473
- I actually did exactly the same thing,

00:59:30.473 --> 00:59:31.911
because she talks over to me,

00:59:31.911 --> 00:59:32.983
and the first thing I did was check

00:59:32.983 --> 00:59:34.928
if there was someone behind me.

00:59:34.928 --> 00:59:36.422
I was like.

00:59:36.422 --> 00:59:38.580
- Yeah, in the UK it's just not a thing.

00:59:38.580 --> 00:59:39.888
You don't talk to people in public.

00:59:39.888 --> 00:59:42.507
And I remember thinking, like,

00:59:42.507 --> 00:59:43.340
oh, uh.

00:59:44.392 --> 00:59:45.437
Yeah.

00:59:45.437 --> 00:59:46.354
Yeah, like,

00:59:47.571 --> 00:59:48.574
what do you want?

00:59:48.574 --> 00:59:49.407
Like?

00:59:49.407 --> 00:59:50.423
Do you want money?

00:59:50.423 --> 00:59:51.810
- Are you begging?

00:59:51.810 --> 00:59:53.150
- You're just like a deer in headlights.

00:59:53.150 --> 00:59:54.864
You just don't know what to do!

00:59:54.864 --> 00:59:55.725
- I know better now.

00:59:55.725 --> 00:59:56.558
- Yeah.

00:59:56.558 --> 00:59:59.070
- I had the craziest fucking Elevator,

00:59:59.070 --> 01:00:00.059
I don't even know if I'm allowed

01:00:00.059 --> 01:00:01.490
to fucking talk about this one.

01:00:01.490 --> 01:00:02.381
- We can cut it.

01:00:02.381 --> 01:00:03.860
- We can cut it if it's too extreme.

01:00:03.860 --> 01:00:06.544
- I mean, it's not the extreme situation.

01:00:06.544 --> 01:00:07.751
It's what the guy said.

01:00:07.751 --> 01:00:09.638
- So he's got a shit in a pumpkin.

01:00:09.638 --> 01:00:10.723
(laughing)

01:00:10.723 --> 01:00:13.322
- No, so it was my first time in LA ever,

01:00:13.322 --> 01:00:15.314
and it was Anime Expo, obviously,

01:00:15.314 --> 01:00:17.224
'cause why else would you go to LA?

01:00:17.224 --> 01:00:19.790
And I was in the hotel, you know.

01:00:19.790 --> 01:00:20.749
Aki was there--

01:00:20.749 --> 01:00:22.258
- I have elevator stories from LA now.

01:00:22.258 --> 01:00:23.907
They're just flashing--

01:00:23.907 --> 01:00:24.740
- It's always LA, man.

01:00:24.740 --> 01:00:25.732
It's always LA.

01:00:25.732 --> 01:00:26.625
But, you know,

01:00:26.625 --> 01:00:28.242
my Japanese side is always like

01:00:28.242 --> 01:00:30.363
if you're just in the
elevator by yourself,

01:00:30.363 --> 01:00:32.479
then you can just be rowdy, and have fun,

01:00:32.479 --> 01:00:33.945
and talk to your friends
and everybody, right?

01:00:33.945 --> 01:00:36.261
But the moment someone
you don't know comes in,

01:00:36.261 --> 01:00:38.558
you gotta behave, you gotta quiet down,

01:00:38.558 --> 01:00:41.358
because you don't want to
inconvenience them, right?

01:00:41.358 --> 01:00:42.257
(laughing)

01:00:42.257 --> 01:00:43.447
I've told you guys this story.

01:00:43.447 --> 01:00:44.280
- Yeah.

01:00:45.137 --> 01:00:46.180
- So it was me, Aki,

01:00:46.180 --> 01:00:48.107
and like a few other people we knew.

01:00:48.107 --> 01:00:49.263
And we were going down in the elevator,

01:00:49.263 --> 01:00:51.323
obviously just chatting it up, whatever.

01:00:51.323 --> 01:00:53.186
Elevator stops halfway.

01:00:53.186 --> 01:00:55.774
Door opens, and this Black guy walks in.

01:00:55.774 --> 01:00:56.877
Don't know him, right?

01:00:56.877 --> 01:00:58.555
So immediately I was like, oh shit,

01:00:58.555 --> 01:00:59.472
someone's, you know,

01:00:59.472 --> 01:01:00.305
coming into the elevator--

01:01:00.305 --> 01:01:01.174
- Let's stop clowning around.

01:01:01.174 --> 01:01:02.007
- Yeah, yeah.

01:01:02.007 --> 01:01:02.840
Let's stop clowning around, you know.

01:01:02.840 --> 01:01:04.121
We don't want to inconvenience him.

01:01:04.121 --> 01:01:05.352
He walks in really quietly.

01:01:05.352 --> 01:01:07.593
Door closes, starts going down,

01:01:07.593 --> 01:01:09.466
and then he just goes, oh yeah,

01:01:09.466 --> 01:01:11.874
everybody shuts up when
the N word walks in.

01:01:11.874 --> 01:01:13.798
(laughing)

01:01:13.798 --> 01:01:15.570
And I was just like,

01:01:15.570 --> 01:01:18.923
I didn't know whether
to say sorry or like?

01:01:18.923 --> 01:01:22.056
'Cause if I said sorry
then we would mean that?

01:01:22.056 --> 01:01:23.318
But I couldn't say anything!

01:01:23.318 --> 01:01:25.294
I couldn't even be like, ahh!

01:01:25.294 --> 01:01:27.007
(laughing)

01:01:27.007 --> 01:01:29.157
So I was just like, eyes darting.

01:01:29.157 --> 01:01:33.511
Just being like, what
am I supposed to say?

01:01:33.511 --> 01:01:34.936
It's like what are you
supposed to say to that,

01:01:34.936 --> 01:01:36.352
in that situation?

01:01:36.352 --> 01:01:37.185
And I was like, man,

01:01:37.185 --> 01:01:38.733
America's fucking terrifying.

01:01:38.733 --> 01:01:40.965
I'm taking the escalator from now on.

01:01:40.965 --> 01:01:43.132
- I've never felt more
complimented in my life

01:01:43.132 --> 01:01:45.720
than when I went into an elevator in LA,

01:01:45.720 --> 01:01:46.881
and there was, like,

01:01:46.881 --> 01:01:48.553
I think there was a bunch of women.

01:01:48.553 --> 01:01:49.940
There must have been five or six of them,

01:01:49.940 --> 01:01:51.956
and they were all mid 40's.

01:01:51.956 --> 01:01:53.262
I don't know what they were doing.

01:01:53.262 --> 01:01:55.654
And they were just saying something,

01:01:55.654 --> 01:01:56.838
and then they asked me a question,

01:01:56.838 --> 01:01:57.868
and I just responded,

01:01:57.868 --> 01:01:59.704
and then when they heard
my voice they were like,

01:01:59.704 --> 01:02:01.073
oh damn!

01:02:01.073 --> 01:02:02.033
(laughing)

01:02:02.033 --> 01:02:04.121
Where are you from?

01:02:04.121 --> 01:02:05.202
And I was like, oh,

01:02:05.202 --> 01:02:06.826
I'm from the UK,

01:02:06.826 --> 01:02:07.682
and they're like, what do you do?

01:02:07.682 --> 01:02:08.982
I was like, I'm a voice actor,

01:02:08.982 --> 01:02:10.105
and they're like, yeah.

01:02:10.105 --> 01:02:10.938
Yeah you are.

01:02:10.938 --> 01:02:13.125
(laughing)

01:02:13.125 --> 01:02:14.719
I was like, oh no.

01:02:14.719 --> 01:02:15.870
I am in danger.

01:02:15.870 --> 01:02:17.353
(laughing)

01:02:17.353 --> 01:02:18.927
But I was so flattered,

01:02:18.927 --> 01:02:21.462
that gave me the confidence
boost I needed that day.

01:02:21.462 --> 01:02:22.312
I was like, hell yeah.

01:02:22.312 --> 01:02:23.145
I'm ready for this panel.

01:02:23.145 --> 01:02:25.680
- When you were in America
with the British accents.

01:02:25.680 --> 01:02:26.784
- [Connor] Yeah, yeah.

01:02:26.784 --> 01:02:28.972
- With any accent that's not American.

01:02:28.972 --> 01:02:29.805
- Yeah, yeah,

01:02:29.805 --> 01:02:31.070
and I think because I
have a deep voice as well,

01:02:31.070 --> 01:02:32.120
it's just the perfect--

01:02:32.120 --> 01:02:33.108
- 'Cause I get that all the time too.

01:02:33.108 --> 01:02:34.813
Like, every time I go to
a Starbucks or whatever,

01:02:34.813 --> 01:02:36.771
and I order something.

01:02:36.771 --> 01:02:39.776
I remember I went to a
Starbucks once in Vegas,

01:02:39.776 --> 01:02:42.101
and I said, I don't remember
when I fucking ordered.

01:02:42.101 --> 01:02:44.597
I was like, can I get a mocha frappuccino,

01:02:44.597 --> 01:02:45.447
or whatever,

01:02:45.447 --> 01:02:47.549
and the girl's like, say that again?

01:02:47.549 --> 01:02:48.443
(laughing)

01:02:48.443 --> 01:02:50.518
And I'm like, and I
thought she didn't hear me!

01:02:50.518 --> 01:02:53.371
So I was like, can I
get a mocha frappuccino?

01:02:53.371 --> 01:02:55.633
And she's like, your accent's so nice,

01:02:55.633 --> 01:02:57.309
I'm gonna have to hear that one more time.

01:02:57.309 --> 01:02:59.583
(laughing)

01:02:59.583 --> 01:03:00.960
- I think I would die inside.

01:03:00.960 --> 01:03:01.793
I'd be like--

01:03:01.793 --> 01:03:02.626
- And I'm just like,

01:03:02.626 --> 01:03:04.084
there's people fucking staring at me.

01:03:04.084 --> 01:03:04.933
I'm just like,

01:03:04.933 --> 01:03:07.104
I just want a fucking mocha frappuccino.

01:03:07.104 --> 01:03:09.036
Just give it to me please.

01:03:09.036 --> 01:03:12.415
So now every time I go to a
Starbucks I'm so afraid of that,

01:03:12.415 --> 01:03:13.248
so I just--

01:03:13.248 --> 01:03:15.412
- You don't order the mocha frappuccino.

01:03:15.412 --> 01:03:16.245
- Yeah.

01:03:16.245 --> 01:03:18.456
No, I just do my best to
do an American accent.

01:03:18.456 --> 01:03:20.155
And they never fucking question me.

01:03:20.155 --> 01:03:21.024
- Americano please.

01:03:21.024 --> 01:03:21.870
- Yeah, I'm just like,

01:03:21.870 --> 01:03:23.158
can I get a latte,

01:03:23.158 --> 01:03:24.172
and they're just like, yeah,

01:03:24.172 --> 01:03:25.106
okay, which one do you want?

01:03:25.106 --> 01:03:28.148
- Do you ever play up your
accent more in the US?

01:03:28.148 --> 01:03:28.981
- Um.

01:03:28.981 --> 01:03:30.452
- I fucking turn that
shit on like a hundred.

01:03:30.452 --> 01:03:33.187
- Yeah, sometimes I do if I
want to get out of a situation,

01:03:33.187 --> 01:03:34.611
where I just start fucking talking,

01:03:34.611 --> 01:03:36.114
like, bogan Australian sometimes,

01:03:36.114 --> 01:03:38.617
where it gets to the
point where they clearly

01:03:38.617 --> 01:03:40.297
don't understand what the fuck I'm saying,

01:03:40.297 --> 01:03:42.229
and I'm just like, (inaudible yelling).

01:03:42.229 --> 01:03:43.863
- I'm out, I'm out.

01:03:43.863 --> 01:03:44.965
- Do you ever go that, Garnt?

01:03:44.965 --> 01:03:46.151
Do you ever turn up your British accent?

01:03:46.151 --> 01:03:47.945
- Um, I mean.

01:03:47.945 --> 01:03:51.328
- I go like full fucking Downton
Abbey in America sometimes.

01:03:51.328 --> 01:03:52.161
- [Garnt] Really?

01:03:52.161 --> 01:03:53.277
- Cause they fucking eat it up, dude.

01:03:53.277 --> 01:03:55.325
Like if I really want
them to be nice to me,

01:03:55.325 --> 01:03:57.437
like the waiter, you know,

01:03:57.437 --> 01:03:59.471
if I want good service, you know?

01:03:59.471 --> 01:04:00.978
I'll be like, thank you so much,

01:04:00.978 --> 01:04:01.853
that's amazing, wow.

01:04:01.853 --> 01:04:02.686
(laughing)

01:04:02.686 --> 01:04:03.519
Wow, thank you.

01:04:03.519 --> 01:04:04.352
This food is delicious.

01:04:04.352 --> 01:04:05.385
You did a great job.

01:04:05.385 --> 01:04:06.396
Oh my gosh.

01:04:06.396 --> 01:04:08.745
- And they're just like, oo.

01:04:08.745 --> 01:04:11.788
- I must sound like such
a fucking asshole though.

01:04:11.788 --> 01:04:13.254
It's fun, it's fun man.

01:04:13.254 --> 01:04:14.120
People are so nice to me--

01:04:14.120 --> 01:04:15.371
- Use it to your advantage, man.

01:04:15.371 --> 01:04:16.204
- I guess so, yeah.

01:04:16.204 --> 01:04:18.955
And then I remember that
Americans would ask me,

01:04:18.955 --> 01:04:19.860
they're like,

01:04:19.860 --> 01:04:21.521
do you guys see American accents the way

01:04:21.521 --> 01:04:22.836
that we see British accents?

01:04:22.836 --> 01:04:24.665
And I'm like, no.

01:04:24.665 --> 01:04:25.498
(laughing)

01:04:25.498 --> 01:04:26.926
Not at all, not at all.

01:04:26.926 --> 01:04:27.819
- Oh, as in attractive?

01:04:27.819 --> 01:04:28.652
- Yeah, yeah,

01:04:28.652 --> 01:04:29.485
yeah, like,

01:04:29.485 --> 01:04:30.318
they were like,

01:04:30.318 --> 01:04:32.371
'cause I remember one time I,

01:04:32.371 --> 01:04:33.391
the way I explained it to him,

01:04:33.391 --> 01:04:36.401
I was like, if there's an
American on public transport,

01:04:36.401 --> 01:04:37.443
everyone knows.

01:04:37.443 --> 01:04:38.276
(laughing)

01:04:38.276 --> 01:04:39.779
Everyone knows and they
know you're American--

01:04:39.779 --> 01:04:40.612
- They're usually the loudest.

01:04:40.612 --> 01:04:41.445
- Yeah, they know.

01:04:41.445 --> 01:04:42.469
They know, they hate it.

01:04:42.469 --> 01:04:44.402
'Cause we're so, like,

01:04:44.402 --> 01:04:47.392
everything we consume
obviously is American media.

01:04:47.392 --> 01:04:49.210
We consume so much American stuff,

01:04:49.210 --> 01:04:51.607
so we're so desensitized
to American media,

01:04:51.607 --> 01:04:53.015
and obviously to American's,

01:04:53.015 --> 01:04:53.848
it's like a, oo,

01:04:53.848 --> 01:04:55.354
it's a flavor of British.

01:04:55.354 --> 01:04:56.478
Hogwarts is interesting.

01:04:56.478 --> 01:04:57.446
- Very international.

01:04:57.446 --> 01:04:58.309
- I think it's also because we've been to

01:04:58.309 --> 01:05:01.003
America so often now for conventions.

01:05:01.003 --> 01:05:02.828
'Cause I remember back
in high school, or--

01:05:02.828 --> 01:05:04.076
- But I think even general British people

01:05:04.076 --> 01:05:06.685
aren't impressed by American's accents.

01:05:06.685 --> 01:05:08.370
- I mean, I remember back in university,

01:05:08.370 --> 01:05:09.755
whenever someone had an American accent

01:05:09.755 --> 01:05:10.831
they would definitely stand out.

01:05:10.831 --> 01:05:12.139
Maybe less so now,

01:05:12.139 --> 01:05:13.884
because I think there's more American's

01:05:13.884 --> 01:05:15.300
coming over to England to study to here.

01:05:15.300 --> 01:05:16.463
- Yeah, we had that one American

01:05:16.463 --> 01:05:18.816
exchange student in our high school,

01:05:18.816 --> 01:05:20.312
and everybody fucking loved it.

01:05:20.312 --> 01:05:21.145
They were like,

01:05:21.145 --> 01:05:22.701
keep talking, keep talking!

01:05:22.701 --> 01:05:23.732
- Maybe things have changed.

01:05:23.732 --> 01:05:24.565
I don't know, man.

01:05:24.565 --> 01:05:26.575
At least in my university,
no one gave a shit.

01:05:26.575 --> 01:05:27.408
- I mean, I definitely,

01:05:27.408 --> 01:05:28.582
I mean, we're all used to them,

01:05:28.582 --> 01:05:29.491
but I think Garnt and I are definitely

01:05:29.491 --> 01:05:31.285
used to it because we
live with an American.

01:05:31.285 --> 01:05:32.118
- Yeah, right.

01:05:32.118 --> 01:05:34.215
I'm definitely used to it now--

01:05:34.215 --> 01:05:35.048
- Yeah, yeah,

01:05:35.048 --> 01:05:35.881
yeah.

01:05:35.881 --> 01:05:36.764
- But before then, it was definitely,

01:05:36.764 --> 01:05:39.308
I do think it was more exotic before I--

01:05:39.308 --> 01:05:42.422
- Because I remember American
accents sounding so harsh.

01:05:42.422 --> 01:05:45.475
Like, you could clearly hear the hard R.

01:05:45.475 --> 01:05:46.308
Like, I mean.

01:05:46.308 --> 01:05:47.141
(laughing)

01:05:47.141 --> 01:05:49.213
- Yo, what is Aki saying?

01:05:49.213 --> 01:05:50.515
Aki canceled?

01:05:50.515 --> 01:05:51.559
(laughing)

01:05:51.559 --> 01:05:53.965
- The hard R in every
word that has an R in it.

01:05:53.965 --> 01:05:55.462
Not just the single word,

01:05:55.462 --> 01:05:58.444
every word that has an R in it.

01:05:58.444 --> 01:06:00.986
Because we don't pronounce
the R's in all of our words,

01:06:00.986 --> 01:06:01.819
right?

01:06:01.819 --> 01:06:05.283
So when we hear the R, like the rrr sound,

01:06:05.283 --> 01:06:06.408
I'm just like--

01:06:06.408 --> 01:06:07.241
- Ew, ew,

01:06:07.241 --> 01:06:08.074
ew, ew.

01:06:08.074 --> 01:06:08.907
- Oh God, why?

01:06:08.907 --> 01:06:09.990
Stop, please.

01:06:11.042 --> 01:06:12.733
- Hearing Americans say British

01:06:12.733 --> 01:06:15.231
swear words is the most disgusting thing--

01:06:15.231 --> 01:06:16.190
- Yeah, we've said this.

01:06:16.190 --> 01:06:17.023
Yeah.

