01:22:20.267 --> 01:22:22.716
so we go to this place and the entire

01:22:22.716 --> 01:22:24.927
menu is handwritten in Kanji.

01:22:24.927 --> 01:22:25.947
- Hell yeah.

01:22:25.947 --> 01:22:27.213
Hell, I love that,

01:22:27.213 --> 01:22:28.401
'cause I've learnt the Kanji,

01:22:28.401 --> 01:22:30.202
the numbers, I'm like (inaudible) brain.

01:22:30.202 --> 01:22:32.137
- But we have to kind of try

01:22:32.137 --> 01:22:34.002
to figure out what everything is.

01:22:34.002 --> 01:22:37.491
And so we go, we pick something that's,

01:22:37.491 --> 01:22:39.663
you know, looks reasonable.

01:22:39.663 --> 01:22:41.058
Because we were looking at the price,

01:22:41.058 --> 01:22:43.525
and the price was about 1300 yen,

01:22:43.525 --> 01:22:45.069
which is about 13 bucks,

01:22:45.069 --> 01:22:48.031
forgetting that in Japan, like,

01:22:48.031 --> 01:22:49.724
ramen is cheap in Japan.

01:22:49.724 --> 01:22:51.037
It's super, super cheap.

01:22:51.037 --> 01:22:52.491
And we were ordering something that was,

01:22:52.491 --> 01:22:54.438
like, 13 bucks when it should have cost--

01:22:54.438 --> 01:22:55.271
- In the middle of nowhere.

01:22:55.271 --> 01:22:56.147
- Yeah, in the middle of nowhere.

01:22:56.147 --> 01:22:56.980
- Should be, like,

01:22:56.980 --> 01:22:57.813
seven, 800 yen?

01:22:57.813 --> 01:23:00.635
- Yeah, when it should be
about seven or 800 yen.

01:23:00.635 --> 01:23:02.127
And we forgot that.

01:23:02.127 --> 01:23:04.748
And I remember we ordered it,

01:23:04.748 --> 01:23:06.571
and the waiter just looks at us.

01:23:06.571 --> 01:23:08.207
And I think he was asking are you sure?

01:23:08.207 --> 01:23:09.950
He was like, are you sure you want this?

01:23:09.950 --> 01:23:10.788
You want this one?

01:23:10.788 --> 01:23:12.643
Two of them, for both of you?

01:23:12.643 --> 01:23:14.483
- You should have known that that point.

01:23:14.483 --> 01:23:15.674
- Yeah, yeah.

01:23:15.674 --> 01:23:17.787
We just want ramen, yeah.

01:23:17.787 --> 01:23:18.620
We want it.

01:23:18.620 --> 01:23:20.479
So he goes back,

01:23:20.479 --> 01:23:23.239
he says something to the chef,

01:23:23.239 --> 01:23:25.378
and the chef's eyes just goes.

01:23:25.378 --> 01:23:26.516
Okay.

01:23:26.516 --> 01:23:27.713
(laughing)

01:23:27.713 --> 01:23:28.806
He was just like, oh,

01:23:28.806 --> 01:23:30.351
you serious, you serious?

01:23:30.351 --> 01:23:33.063
- They get both their keys
out and unlock the safe.

01:23:33.063 --> 01:23:35.224
- Crack the neck.

01:23:35.224 --> 01:23:39.818
- So what comes out is they
bring us this extra large ramen,

01:23:39.818 --> 01:23:44.818
and then with it was just
this extra large beef ball.

01:23:44.944 --> 01:23:47.039
And then he brings out one of them,

01:23:47.039 --> 01:23:48.223
puts it in front of me,

01:23:48.223 --> 01:23:50.638
and I just think, I've
made a massive mistake.

01:23:50.638 --> 01:23:51.471
(laughing)

01:23:51.471 --> 01:23:52.304
I look at Sydney.

01:23:52.304 --> 01:23:53.342
Sydney's just staring at this ball,

01:23:53.342 --> 01:23:54.175
being like--

01:23:54.175 --> 01:23:55.008
- That's coming, that's coming!

01:23:55.008 --> 01:23:57.192
- Sydney's like, we ordered two of those.

01:23:57.192 --> 01:23:58.324
One each.

01:23:58.324 --> 01:24:01.666
'Cause it would be impossible
for one of us to finish this,

01:24:01.666 --> 01:24:05.249
let alone two of us
finishing both of them.

01:24:07.107 --> 01:24:09.183
And so he brings it over to Sydney,

01:24:09.183 --> 01:24:10.328
and I don't know what the etiquette

01:24:10.328 --> 01:24:11.757
is if you don't finish your food,

01:24:11.757 --> 01:24:14.953
but we fucking tried to
devour as much as we can.

01:24:14.953 --> 01:24:16.355
We don't even get through half of it.

01:24:16.355 --> 01:24:17.188
- Oh my God.

01:24:17.188 --> 01:24:19.493
- And we feel so fucking bad.

01:24:19.493 --> 01:24:20.892
And we're getting the bill,

01:24:20.892 --> 01:24:23.118
it was the most shameful bill of all time.

01:24:23.118 --> 01:24:24.327
I'm like, it's,

01:24:24.327 --> 01:24:26.420
(speaking in foreign language).

01:24:26.420 --> 01:24:27.428
- He's like, are you sure about that?

01:24:27.428 --> 01:24:28.683
Are you sure?

01:24:28.683 --> 01:24:30.264
- Okay bitch.

01:24:30.264 --> 01:24:32.545
- We didn't even make
a fucking dent in this.

01:24:32.545 --> 01:24:33.529
- Oh my God.

01:24:33.529 --> 01:24:36.461
I have never experienced
that because I would rather

01:24:36.461 --> 01:24:39.201
behead myself that leave
food in a Japanese place.

01:24:39.201 --> 01:24:41.028
I don't know why I'm so scared of it?

01:24:41.028 --> 01:24:43.146
Like one time, in Matsuya funnily enough,

01:24:43.146 --> 01:24:46.503
I accidentally ordered two
of the double L sized sets?

01:24:46.503 --> 01:24:47.336
- [Joey] Right.

01:24:47.336 --> 01:24:48.169
- Which is like--

01:24:48.169 --> 01:24:49.224
- Way too much food for one person.

01:24:49.224 --> 01:24:50.953
- I think it's near 4000 calories.

01:24:50.953 --> 01:24:53.059
Like it is a mountain of rice.

01:24:53.059 --> 01:24:55.225
And I don't know how I actually did this,

01:24:55.225 --> 01:24:56.914
I should have realized by how much I paid,

01:24:56.914 --> 01:24:57.747
and it came,

01:24:57.747 --> 01:24:59.236
and I was like, fuck.

01:24:59.236 --> 01:25:00.758
I wasn't even that hungry.

01:25:00.758 --> 01:25:02.074
I was like, shit.

01:25:02.074 --> 01:25:05.056
So I forced this inside of me,

01:25:05.056 --> 01:25:08.443
and I was, when I got home I threw up.

01:25:08.443 --> 01:25:11.280
But in the restaurant I was like,

01:25:11.280 --> 01:25:13.255
if you can imagine a dude,

01:25:13.255 --> 01:25:15.095
literally like if his esophagus was full,

01:25:15.095 --> 01:25:15.928
I was literally like.

01:25:15.928 --> 01:25:18.365
(laughing)

01:25:18.365 --> 01:25:21.368
Like drinking the miso
soup to push it down.

01:25:21.368 --> 01:25:22.201
You know what I mean?

01:25:22.201 --> 01:25:23.179
I was like, give me more water.

01:25:23.179 --> 01:25:25.183
I need to push this shit down with water.

01:25:25.183 --> 01:25:26.262
It was horrible.

01:25:26.262 --> 01:25:27.417
I thought I was gonna die.

01:25:27.417 --> 01:25:28.450
They must have been looking at me,

01:25:28.450 --> 01:25:30.356
like, at me crying at a Matsuya,

01:25:30.356 --> 01:25:33.606
like why is he still eating it?

01:25:33.606 --> 01:25:35.937
- That's just the most
British thing I've ever heard.

01:25:35.937 --> 01:25:38.287
Would rather throw up
from eating too much food

01:25:38.287 --> 01:25:40.776
than feel the shame of
leaving food on the plate.

01:25:40.776 --> 01:25:43.154
- Yeah, I would rather
throw up in an alleyway

01:25:43.154 --> 01:25:46.488
than order way too much, clearly,

01:25:46.488 --> 01:25:47.980
and then have to give them it back,

01:25:47.980 --> 01:25:49.288
and be like, throw it away.

01:25:49.288 --> 01:25:50.121
- [Garnt] Yeah.

01:25:50.121 --> 01:25:50.954
- Yeah, okay,

01:25:50.954 --> 01:25:53.621
was it very unhealthy and
extremely questionable?

01:25:53.621 --> 01:25:56.321
Yeah, but sometimes you have
to make a decision in life.

01:25:56.321 --> 01:25:58.183
- But I got the respect
from those Matsuya--

01:25:58.183 --> 01:25:59.950
- When I say (speaking
in foreign language),

01:25:59.950 --> 01:26:01.278
I fucking meant that shit.

01:26:01.278 --> 01:26:03.528
(laughing)

01:26:04.538 --> 01:26:06.107
I'm walking out like.

01:26:06.107 --> 01:26:08.340
(laughing)

01:26:08.340 --> 01:26:09.173
Oh God.

01:26:10.037 --> 01:26:12.791
My bowls stacked on top of each other.

01:26:12.791 --> 01:26:14.477
I'd never eaten that much food in my life.

01:26:14.477 --> 01:26:16.332
- I'll tell you the one
place I don't feel shameful

01:26:16.332 --> 01:26:17.726
for leaving food on the plate though,

01:26:17.726 --> 01:26:19.473
and that's whenever I go to America.

01:26:19.473 --> 01:26:20.306
- Oh yeah, yeah,

01:26:20.306 --> 01:26:21.139
yeah--

01:26:21.139 --> 01:26:24.473
- And just witness the food
sizes there for everything.

01:26:24.473 --> 01:26:26.898
- I had that in fucking Chicago

01:26:26.898 --> 01:26:28.440
when I was at Con+Alt+Delete.

01:26:28.440 --> 01:26:29.680
- I'm sure it's no surprise

01:26:29.680 --> 01:26:31.765
to Americans that their
food portions are--

01:26:31.765 --> 01:26:32.912
- Yeah, and I'm just like,

01:26:32.912 --> 01:26:34.302
I had that in Chicago when I ordered

01:26:34.302 --> 01:26:36.018
deep dish pizza for the first time,

01:26:36.018 --> 01:26:38.008
and because we'd never ordered it, right,

01:26:38.008 --> 01:26:39.134
and most of us never ordered it,

01:26:39.134 --> 01:26:40.022
we were like, oh yeah,

01:26:40.022 --> 01:26:41.168
it's just the same as a regular pizza.

01:26:41.168 --> 01:26:42.038
There's like, what?

01:26:42.038 --> 01:26:43.153
Seven of us there?

01:26:43.153 --> 01:26:45.699
Yeah, we'll get five deep dish pizzas.

01:26:45.699 --> 01:26:46.651
- It looks awful.

01:26:46.651 --> 01:26:47.484
Am I crazy?

01:26:47.484 --> 01:26:49.133
Does it taste terrible?

01:26:49.133 --> 01:26:50.294
- It tastes good, but--

01:26:50.294 --> 01:26:51.985
- It tastes great for the first slice.

01:26:51.985 --> 01:26:54.753
- Yeah, but one slice is
like eating a whole pizza.

01:26:54.753 --> 01:26:55.586
Basically.

01:26:55.586 --> 01:26:58.247
Because it's literally just a whole pizza

01:26:58.247 --> 01:27:00.353
just stacked on top of one slice.

01:27:00.353 --> 01:27:02.690
- I've had the kind of deep ones,

01:27:02.690 --> 01:27:04.219
but not like there where it looks like--

01:27:04.219 --> 01:27:06.102
- Oh no, we had the fucking deep dish.

01:27:06.102 --> 01:27:08.725
- It's basically a basin
for the sauce, right?

01:27:08.725 --> 01:27:09.673
Like it's?

01:27:09.673 --> 01:27:11.466
- It's a pizza lasagna, that's what is it.

01:27:11.466 --> 01:27:13.321
- But at that point it's like the whole,

01:27:13.321 --> 01:27:16.701
the best part of the pizza
is the synergy between--

01:27:16.701 --> 01:27:17.870
- The synergy? (laughing)

01:27:17.870 --> 01:27:19.865
- The synergy.

01:27:19.865 --> 01:27:22.217
- What are you talking about?

01:27:22.217 --> 01:27:23.848
- Bro, the way the bread,

01:27:23.848 --> 01:27:26.459
the cheese and the sauce
is the perfect amount?

01:27:26.459 --> 01:27:27.697
You get the best bite.

01:27:27.697 --> 01:27:29.928
If there was one too
many of those elements--

01:27:29.928 --> 01:27:32.180
- It's like a fucking pizza
theologist right here.

01:27:32.180 --> 01:27:33.013
- Dude.

01:27:33.013 --> 01:27:33.846
I'm telling you, man.

01:27:33.846 --> 01:27:36.942
If there's too much sauce,
you got to drink the pizza.

01:27:36.942 --> 01:27:37.779
What's up with that?

01:27:37.779 --> 01:27:38.980
- I like the saucy pizza's though?

01:27:38.980 --> 01:27:39.813
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah.

01:27:39.813 --> 01:27:40.646
- [Connor] No, no.

01:27:40.646 --> 01:27:41.479
- Like the extra sauce pizza's.

01:27:41.479 --> 01:27:43.879
But I will admit that deep dish was,

01:27:43.879 --> 01:27:44.875
like, damn.

01:27:44.875 --> 01:27:47.105
- Could you put a straw
in it and drink it?

01:27:47.105 --> 01:27:48.087
- Probably.

01:27:48.087 --> 01:27:49.575
- That shouldn't happen,
that shouldn't be possible--

01:27:49.575 --> 01:27:50.535
- I mean, it goes in layers.

01:27:50.535 --> 01:27:52.528
I didn't realize why so many Americans

01:27:52.528 --> 01:27:56.398
called pizza's pies until
I had a deep dish pizza,

01:27:56.398 --> 01:27:57.530
and I was like, oh,

01:27:57.530 --> 01:27:59.232
this is a fucking pie.

01:27:59.232 --> 01:28:00.397
- This is a pizza pie.

01:28:00.397 --> 01:28:01.448
- Is that where it came from?

01:28:01.448 --> 01:28:02.498
- Yeah, I think so?

01:28:02.498 --> 01:28:03.514
- I'm not sure,

01:28:03.514 --> 01:28:05.499
but I was definitely eating a pie

01:28:05.499 --> 01:28:07.961
that was shaped like a pizza.

01:28:07.961 --> 01:28:09.213
- A pizza flavored pie.

01:28:09.213 --> 01:28:10.051
- Yeah, exactly.

01:28:10.051 --> 01:28:11.265
- Pretty much, exactly.

01:28:11.265 --> 01:28:12.098
- But I remember as well,

01:28:12.098 --> 01:28:13.705
when I went to Texas for the first time,

01:28:13.705 --> 01:28:14.538
and we went to, like,

01:28:14.538 --> 01:28:15.923
I don't remember what the
Italian restaurant was,

01:28:15.923 --> 01:28:17.610
but it was a big Italian restaurant.

01:28:17.610 --> 01:28:19.348
And portion sizes in America--

01:28:19.348 --> 01:28:20.531
- Olive Garden?
- No.

01:28:20.531 --> 01:28:21.974
(laughing)

01:28:21.974 --> 01:28:24.626
Portion sizes in America
are already big, right?

01:28:24.626 --> 01:28:28.633
But in Texas it's hold my
beer levels on fucking food.

01:28:28.633 --> 01:28:29.986
So we went to this Italian restaurant,

01:28:29.986 --> 01:28:32.581
and it was Misty's birthday.

01:28:32.581 --> 01:28:34.018
So we went to an Italian restaurant,

01:28:34.018 --> 01:28:36.184
and we were getting all this food,

01:28:36.184 --> 01:28:37.017
and, you know,

01:28:37.017 --> 01:28:39.210
normally when you go in an
Italian restaurant anywhere,

01:28:39.210 --> 01:28:42.197
right, it's like you order
one bowl of pasta each,

01:28:42.197 --> 01:28:43.276
whatever you want.

01:28:43.276 --> 01:28:45.171
Maybe share it around or whatever, no.

01:28:45.171 --> 01:28:46.716
In this Italian restaurant it's like

01:28:46.716 --> 01:28:51.549
one dish of pasta can feed an
Ethiopian family for a year.

01:28:53.490 --> 01:28:55.322
Like, it is insane,

01:28:55.322 --> 01:28:57.285
it's too much pasta.

01:28:57.285 --> 01:28:58.970
And we thought that
was already ridiculous.

01:28:58.970 --> 01:29:00.098
Like, we couldn't even finish that shit.

01:29:00.098 --> 01:29:02.349
But then we wanted to order a cake, right?

01:29:02.349 --> 01:29:03.291
And we saw, oh,

01:29:03.291 --> 01:29:05.078
they sell tiramisu here.

01:29:05.078 --> 01:29:05.911
And Misty's like, yeah,

01:29:05.911 --> 01:29:07.504
I want a tiramisu!

01:29:07.504 --> 01:29:09.301
And normally when you order cake

01:29:09.301 --> 01:29:11.465
at a restaurant it's
like one slice, right?

01:29:11.465 --> 01:29:12.298
- Yeah.

01:29:12.298 --> 01:29:13.981
- No, they brought out
the whole fucking cake.

01:29:13.981 --> 01:29:14.840
It was like.

01:29:14.840 --> 01:29:16.087
(laughing)

01:29:16.087 --> 01:29:18.066
It was legitimately this big!

01:29:18.066 --> 01:29:19.890
This big and this deep.

01:29:19.890 --> 01:29:20.870
- How much was it?

01:29:20.870 --> 01:29:22.693
- It was like 20 bucks.
- What the fuck.

01:29:22.693 --> 01:29:25.709
- And I was just like, I
think we ordered wrong?

01:29:25.709 --> 01:29:26.696
And they were like, no,

01:29:26.696 --> 01:29:29.517
there's only one tiramisu on the menu,

01:29:29.517 --> 01:29:30.483
so it must mean this!

01:29:30.483 --> 01:29:31.851
- Just ordering a cake.

01:29:31.851 --> 01:29:33.330
- That's just like the only option

01:29:33.330 --> 01:29:34.624
of anything is a crate of it.

01:29:34.624 --> 01:29:37.061
Sometimes I just want a bit of it.

01:29:37.061 --> 01:29:37.994
- And I'm just like?

01:29:37.994 --> 01:29:39.294
And I thought like, oh,

01:29:39.294 --> 01:29:40.530
you know, maybe it's a little bit.

01:29:40.530 --> 01:29:42.144
Maybe it's like a really fancy tiramisu,

01:29:42.144 --> 01:29:43.280
right, because of the price?

01:29:43.280 --> 01:29:46.174
But I wasn't expecting
fucking grandma to bust

01:29:46.174 --> 01:29:48.196
into the fucking
restaurant just being like,

01:29:48.196 --> 01:29:49.376
here you go!

01:29:49.376 --> 01:29:51.603
- Sometimes when I'm with
Americans in America,

01:29:51.603 --> 01:29:52.436
and they're like, yeah,

01:29:52.436 --> 01:29:53.277
that place is way too expensive.

01:29:53.277 --> 01:29:54.214
You get ripped off.

01:29:54.214 --> 01:29:55.123
And I'm like, bro,

01:29:55.123 --> 01:29:57.061
I got enough to feed my whole family.

01:29:57.061 --> 01:29:58.045
What do you mean?

01:29:58.045 --> 01:29:58.990
In my head I'm like, mate,

01:29:58.990 --> 01:29:59.973
you didn't get ripped off.

01:29:59.973 --> 01:30:01.395
You been to France, bro?

01:30:01.395 --> 01:30:03.546
You get one string of pasta and sauce,

01:30:03.546 --> 01:30:05.487
and they charge you $20 for that shit.

01:30:05.487 --> 01:30:07.596
- Would you like six snails for 20 euros?

01:30:07.596 --> 01:30:08.429
- Yeah, I'm like?

01:30:08.429 --> 01:30:11.577
In Europe, you don't
get that for that much.

01:30:11.577 --> 01:30:12.588
It's rare, like,

01:30:12.588 --> 01:30:13.722
I mean, to me,

01:30:13.722 --> 01:30:15.951
yeah, LA was super expensive,

01:30:15.951 --> 01:30:18.087
but I always got a shit
ton of food so I was fine.

01:30:18.087 --> 01:30:19.229
- Yeah, exactly--

01:30:19.229 --> 01:30:21.065
- I remember having to learn the hard way

01:30:21.065 --> 01:30:23.000
that you just never order appetizers

01:30:23.000 --> 01:30:25.217
when you go to an American restaurant,

01:30:25.217 --> 01:30:26.050
'cause there's been--

01:30:26.050 --> 01:30:26.883
- It's a meal.

01:30:26.883 --> 01:30:29.314
- Yeah, because why would
you call it appetizers

01:30:29.314 --> 01:30:31.740
when it's as big as the main course?

01:30:31.740 --> 01:30:32.894
I don't get it.

01:30:32.894 --> 01:30:34.885
In every other part of the world,

01:30:34.885 --> 01:30:35.819
you order appetizer,

01:30:35.819 --> 01:30:37.788
you have a three course meal sometimes,

01:30:37.788 --> 01:30:38.847
you know, if you're feeling frisky.

01:30:38.847 --> 01:30:40.960
In America you order
one thing off the menu,

01:30:40.960 --> 01:30:43.581
and that one thing can feed
a fucking family for a week.

01:30:43.581 --> 01:30:44.414
I swear to God.

01:30:44.414 --> 01:30:46.540
- One thing I could never
fucking believe was the concept

01:30:46.540 --> 01:30:49.575
of bottomless fries at
a fast food restaurant.

01:30:49.575 --> 01:30:50.640
- Bottomless everything.

01:30:50.640 --> 01:30:51.473
- Bottomless everything.

01:30:51.473 --> 01:30:52.399
Already, like,

01:30:52.399 --> 01:30:55.172
free refills was like a whoa concept,

01:30:55.172 --> 01:30:57.006
because in Australia there's no fucking

01:30:57.006 --> 01:30:57.884
